# Thread gem for ORuby

This gem provides limited compatibility for code that uses the main Ruby thread
identity. It does not provide Ruby shared-heap threads.

## Compatibility

`Thread.new`, `Thread.start`, and `Thread.go` are unsupported and raise
`NotImplementedError`; they no longer create cloned-state workers. This is a
breaking change for code that used these entry points. `Process.detach` is also
unsupported because its `core_ext` implementation calls `Thread.new`.

`Thread.current` and `Thread.main` remain available and return the same main
thread object for a state. When `core_ext` is loaded, its thread-local methods,
such as `Thread.current[:key]`, remain available on that object. The retained
`Mutex`, `Queue`, and `SizedQueue` classes have not been certified for
correctness by this change; their presence is not a concurrency guarantee.

An `MrbState` must not be accessed concurrently from multiple goroutines. The
experimental [isolated worker gem](../isolated_worker/README.md) provides a
separate, opt-in API for work in isolated mruby heaps, not a replacement for
Ruby threads. Its README describes the worker API and its limits.

The existing clone machinery is retained for future fork-like research only;
it is not an OS fork or a process API.

## Install

```go
import _ "github.com/oruby/oruby/gem/thread"
```

